No enterprise code or assets were used.

No font or image asset files were copied.
The package ships Geist Variable Latin as
  dist/assets/geist-latin-wght-normal-BgDaEnEv.woff2 (29,400 bytes),
but its own redistribution license text was not present in the inspected
dist assets. Bot for Orca uses OpenMausBot's fallback font stack instead:
-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif.

OpenMausBot's procedural mascot component in PlacesRail-Bg3fXQbs.js uses
bot.color, mascotBody and mascotFaceColor (plus appearance preferences),
not a deterministic colour derived from the bot ID. These fields are not
available in Bot for Orca's existing roster protocol. To preserve the protocol,
Bot for Orca retains its original generated SVG avatars and stored-image support,
including working animation and reduced-motion handling.

